            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioner, the case turns on whether a non\u2011citizen may collaterally attack a removal order under 8\u202fU.S.C.\u202f\u00a7\u202f1326(d) without showing (1) exhaustion of any available administrative remedies, (2) that the removal proceedings improperly deprived him of the right to judicial review, or (3) that the entry of the order was fundamentally unfair."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Background and Question Presented",
