  "oral_argument": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "443db17cf31b1df30f013ad8aaeab15f42366d4d44b9c24df3c0fec2d4a784a8",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-443db17cf31b-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kagan, justice Kagan: Suppose the immigration judge said there is no administrative procedure to appeal; would the provision be satisfied?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "443db17cf31b1df30f013ad8aaeab15f42366d4d44b9c24df3c0fec2d4a784a8",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-443db17cf31b-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 23,
              "start": 23
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kagan, justice Kagan: How is that distinguishable from this case? Because, in this case, there's just as much an error in the first \u2013 from the IJ."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "443db17cf31b1df30f013ad8aaeab15f42366d4d44b9c24df3c0fec2d4a784a8",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-443db17cf31b-0001-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 31,
              "start": 31
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Thomas, justice Thomas: Is it your argument that the administrative remedies are so complicated that they would always be unavailable?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "443db17cf31b1df30f013ad8aaeab15f42366d4d44b9c24df3c0fec2d4a784a8",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-443db17cf31b-0001-0007"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 34,
              "start": 34
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Breyer, justice Breyer: How, in your opinion, at the risk of repetition, do you get out of this?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "443db17cf31b1df30f013ad8aaeab15f42366d4d44b9c24df3c0fec2d4a784a8",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-443db17cf31b-0001-0008"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 37,
              "start": 37
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Alito, justice Alito: Suppose Leocal and the Ninth Circuit decision had not been decided; could your client have moved to dismiss the indictment on the grounds that the prior removal order was invalid?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "443db17cf31b1df30f013ad8aaeab15f42366d4d44b9c24df3c0fec2d4a784a8",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-443db17cf31b-0001-0009"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 40,
              "start": 40
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Alito, justice Alito: Do you accept the validity of the deportation order?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "443db17cf31b1df30f013ad8aaeab15f42366d4d44b9c24df3c0fec2d4a784a8",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-443db17cf31b-0001-0012"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 43,
              "start": 43
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kagan, justice Kagan: Is this essentially a misrepresentation case, as described in Ross, so that even if there was an administrative remedy on the books, it wasn\u2019t truly available?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "443db17cf31b1df30f013ad8aaeab15f42366d4d44b9c24df3c0fec2d4a784a8",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-443db17cf31b-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 46,
              "start": 46
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Barrett, justice Barrett: Does availability under 1326(d) vary according to the difficulty of the law that underlay the initial conviction?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "443db17cf31b1df30f013ad8aaeab15f42366d4d44b9c24df3c0fec2d4a784a8",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-443db17cf31b-0000-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Chief Justice Roberts, chief Justice Roberts: We will hear argument next in Case 20\u2011437, United States versus Palomar\u2011Santiago."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "443db17cf31b1df30f013ad8aaeab15f42366d4d44b9c24df3c0fec2d4a784a8",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-443db17cf31b-0002-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 48,
              "start": 48
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Chief Justice Roberts, chief Justice Roberts: A minute to wrap up, Mr. Garcia."
      }
    ],
