  "overview": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1faec98fee6a72194cbb4d76cda220d615b520c36de727728fc8f6389577a812",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1faec98fee6a-0000-0000",
              "ev-1faec98fee6a-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 2,
              "start": 2
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Palomar\u2011Santiago, a Mexican national living in the United States, was convicted in California state court of a felony DUI in 1988, which was treated as an aggravated felony subject to removal under 8\u202fU.S.C.\u202f\u00a7\u202f1227(a)(2)(A)(iii)."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1faec98fee6a72194cbb4d76cda220d615b520c36de727728fc8f6389577a812",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1faec98fee6a-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 2,
              "start": 2
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "He was removed after a hearing before an immigration judge and waived his right to appeal."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1faec98fee6a72194cbb4d76cda220d615b520c36de727728fc8f6389577a812",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1faec98fee6a-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 2,
              "start": 2
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "In 2017 Palomar\u2011Santiago was found in the United States and indicted on one count of unlawful reentry after removal."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1faec98fee6a72194cbb4d76cda220d615b520c36de727728fc8f6389577a812",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1faec98fee6a-0000-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 10,
              "start": 10
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Supreme Court reversed the Ninth Circuit\u2019s judgment and remanded the case for further proceedings consistent with this opinion."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Overview",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
  "party_positions": [
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "443db17cf31b1df30f013ad8aaeab15f42366d4d44b9c24df3c0fec2d4a784a8",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-443db17cf31b-0000-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 4,
                "start": 4
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner, section\u202f1326(d) resolves the question presented in this case."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "United States (Petitioner)",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Respondent",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "443db17cf31b1df30f013ad8aaeab15f42366d4d44b9c24df3c0fec2d4a784a8",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-443db17cf31b-0001-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 25,
                "start": 25
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Respondent, section\u202f1326(d)\u2019s text is clear; the immigration judge\u2019s finding that the prior offense qualified as an aggravated felony does not satisfy the statutory requirements of exhaustion, deprivation of review, or fundamental unfairness."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Bradley N. Garcia",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "443db17cf31b1df30f013ad8aaeab15f42366d4d44b9c24df3c0fec2d4a784a8",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-443db17cf31b-0001-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 26,
                "start": 26
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Bradley N. Garcia, the indictment should be dismissed because a Section\u202f1326 prosecution cannot proceed based on an invalid removal order, and the invalidity of the order here is undisputed."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Respondent",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "443db17cf31b1df30f013ad8aaeab15f42366d4d44b9c24df3c0fec2d4a784a8",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-443db17cf31b-0002-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 44,
                "start": 44
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Respondent, there was a misrepresentation, and the categorical approach is so opaque that no reasonable non\u2011citizen can use it."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Palomar\u2011Santiago (Respondent)",
      "status": "complete",
